<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/establishes> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/establishes> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "UNUSED. Declared to name the shape of the relation, not to license it: nothing in this repo may derive this edge."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/establishes> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Evidence>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/establishes> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "establishes"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/evaluation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/evaluation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The Stage 0 measurement artefacts, in the graph rather than beside it.\n\nThis module is not in the roadmap's module list and it earns its place: it is\nwhat lets a prohibited output be a node with edges instead of a paragraph in a\nYAML file. PU-0004 says that attributing the Manual's 'obvious, direct and\nimmediate' formulation to the Act is prohibited and that the error is\nstructurally detectable. It is only structurally detectable if the prohibition,\nthe question it attaches to, and the passages involved are all in the same\ngraph. Here they are, and `shapes/prohibited-use.ttl` reads them."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/evaluation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "TM-Knowledge — evaluation module"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/evaluation> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#imports> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/provenance>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/evaluation> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#versionInfo> "draft — not approved"  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/evidence> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/evidence> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Entirely unpopulated, and the emptiest module in the draft on purpose.**\n\nThe roadmap names it and the approved section 43 set says almost nothing about\nevidence: the pilot's material is about what a sign connotes, not about what an\napplicant files to establish something. Two records touch it — written\npermission overcoming a ground (GR-0039), information establishing that an\napplicant is the owner of a phoneword (GX-0010) — and neither is enough to\nmodel an evidence taxonomy from.\n\nPopulating this is a Part 22/23 job (evidence of use under s 41), and Part 22 is\nexplicitly out of the pilot scope draft. Left declared so the module list is\ncomplete and so nobody builds a second one."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/evidence> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "TM-Knowledge — evidence module"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/evidence> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#imports> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/legal-concepts>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/evidence> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#versionInfo> "draft — not approved · unpopulated"  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/examination> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/examination> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Who does what, and to what.\n\nAlmost entirely **declared and unpopulated**, and that is the honest state: the\napproved set describes what the Manual says about section 43, not a process\nmodel of examination, and inventing one would be authoring practice.\n\nThe role classes below are here for a specific reason. The reviewer's covering\nnote (`review/returned/260826-expert-feedback.md`, HANDOFF Q17) named nine terms\nthat need high-level definitions — Registrar, Delegate, Examiner, Decision\nMaker, Office Practice, Subject Matter Expert, Oppositions, Grounds for\nRejection, Adverse Report — because the seed vocabulary was drawn from Part 29\nalone and gives a narrow view of the roles. Declaring the classes empty is how\nthat gap is made visible in the model rather than only in a document. Note also\nQ-28: a term's definition is usually not in a passage that cites anything, so\nADR-0022's scope rule will not find these on its own."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/examination> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "TM-Knowledge — examination module"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/examination> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#imports> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/legal-concepts>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/examination> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#versionInfo> "draft — not approved"  .
