<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/excludesBasis> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/usedBy> "GR-0056"  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/expectedConclusion> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/expectedConclusion> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ReasoningExpectation>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/expectedConclusion> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "expected conclusion"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/expectedConclusion> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/expectsBoundaryLabel> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/expectsBoundaryLabel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A label the question expects that the vocabulary deliberately excludes.\n\nThe distinction this draws is the difference between a hole and an edge. A\nlabel matching no concept usually means the vocabulary is short something. But\nwhere an approved concept records that same label under `not_labels` — the\nfield the schema calls the most valuable on the record — the vocabulary has\nalready said, in a record somebody signed, that the term belongs elsewhere. The\nquestion is then naming the boundary it tests, not asking for a missing concept.\n\n`deceptively similar` on CQ-0007 is the case that forced it: three approved\nconcepts exclude the term, and CQ-0007 asks \"confusion between my mark and\nsomeone else's — which section is that?\", whose answer is section 44. Counted\nas a gap, it reported a miss that was not a miss on every measurement. The\nowner ruled on OQ-0002: \"It belongs to section 44 — keep it out, the question\nis using it as a boundary marker\" (ADR-0075)."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/expectsBoundaryLabel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "expects boundary label"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/expectsBoundaryLabel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/expectsConcept> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/expectsConcept> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The concept a question expects an answer to engage, resolved from the label the\nrecord carries.\n\nResolution is exact string equality against a `skos:prefLabel` or a\n`skos:altLabel` — a lookup, not a reading. A label that matches nothing gets\ntmk:expectsConceptLabel and no edge, and is reported: an approximate match here\nwould silently attach a question to the wrong concept, and `deceptively similar`\nagainst `likely to deceive or cause confusion` is exactly the pair that would\ngo wrong first."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/expectsConcept> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "expects concept"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/expectsConcept> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/LegalConcept>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/expectsConceptLabel> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/expectsConceptLabel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The label as the record wrote it, kept whether or not it resolved. An unresolved one is either a boundary (see below) or a worklist item: the vocabulary is missing a concept, or the question names one by a variant nobody has recorded as an alt label."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/expectsConceptLabel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "expects concept label"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/expectsConceptLabel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/expertShouldCheck> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/expertShouldCheck> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The specific thing most likely to be wrong here. A pointer, not a disclaimer."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/expertShouldCheck> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Assertion>  .
