<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/lastAmended> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/lastAmended> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The Manual page's own amendment note where it carries one. Page-level and self-reported — not a version stamp, and not comparable across pages."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/lastAmended> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Page>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/lastAmended> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "last amended"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/lastAmended> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/legal-concepts> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/legal-concepts> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The concept layer, and the module with the largest declared-but-unpopulated\npart of the model.\n\nEvery approved concept in `eval/gold/concepts.yaml` becomes a `tmk:LegalConcept`.\nWhether it is also one of the four subclasses below — GroundOfRefusal, LegalTest,\nRelevantFactor, Exception — depends on a signed record in\n`eval/gold/concept-types.yaml`, and on nothing else. Deciding that 'connotation'\nis a LegalTest rather than a RelevantFactor is a legal judgement this repo may\nnot make (CLAUDE.md rule 1); what it may do is hold the answer somebody gives.\n\nThe owner confirmed the four groups on 2026-09-08 (OQ-0001) and the container\nnow exists (ADR-0071). Until a concept has a type record it stays a bare\n`tmk:LegalConcept`, and the count of unsorted concepts is reported by every\nbuild rather than defaulted away. A machine filling these would produce a\ntaxonomy that reads as authoritative and was authored by nobody."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/legal-concepts> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "TM-Knowledge — legal concepts module"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/legal-concepts> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#imports> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/authority>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/legal-concepts> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#versionInfo> "draft — not approved"  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/legislativeBasis> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/legislativeBasis> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The provision the concept operates under. A concept can have a legislative basis and still be a creature of practice — the basis says which ground it belongs to, not that the Act uses the word."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/legislativeBasis> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/LegalConcept>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/legislativeBasis> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "legislative basis"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/legislativeBasis> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/LegislativeProvision>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/mayGiveRiseTo> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/mayGiveRiseTo> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ApprovedRelation>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/mayGiveRiseTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Approved usage: 6 relationships (GR-0007, GR-0024, GR-0037, GR-0044, GR-0048, GR-0057)."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/mayGiveRiseTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/LegalMatter>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/mayGiveRiseTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "may give rise to"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/mayGiveRiseTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/LegalMatter>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/mayGiveRiseTo> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/observedObjectType> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/LegalConcept>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/mayGiveRiseTo> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/observedObjectType> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/LegislativeProvision>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/mayGiveRiseTo> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/observedSubjectType> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/LegalConcept>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/mayGiveRiseTo> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/usageCount> "6"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/mayGiveRiseTo> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/usedBy> "GR-0007"  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/mayGiveRiseTo> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/usedBy> "GR-0024"  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/mayGiveRiseTo> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/usedBy> "GR-0037"  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/mayGiveRiseTo> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/usedBy> "GR-0044"  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/mayGiveRiseTo> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/usedBy> "GR-0048"  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/mayGiveRiseTo> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/usedBy> "GR-0057"  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/mention> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/mention> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The surface text upstream matched, where it recorded one."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/mention> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Citation>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/mention> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "mention"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/mention> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/mentionClass> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/mentionClass> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The expert's type for the mention, as the class itself rather than as a string.\n\nAsserted on the *mention*, never on the thing mentioned. A mention typed\nManualInstruction says a person read that span as a statement of practice; it\ndoes not say the chunk containing it is one, and it must not, because\ntmk:ManualInstruction and tmk:LegislativeProvision are disjoint and a chunk\nquoting the Act contains both."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/mentionClass> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/EntityMention>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/mentionClass> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "mention class"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/mentionType> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/mentionType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The expert's type for the mention: LegalConcept, ManualInstruction, LegislativeProvision, Role, Date, Other. Recorded as given — an agent may not retype a mention."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/mentionType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/EntityMention>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/mentionType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "mention type"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/mentionType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/mixedAuthority> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/mixedAuthority> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Derived by RULE-0001. The passage contains both quoted legislative text and\nthe Registrar's own practice, so any output derived from it must keep the two\ndistinguishable.\n\nThis is GX-0001's expected inference, and the reason it matters is CQ-0001's\ncaveat: the Manual quotes s 43 in full inside TMM/Part29/1#1, so an answer can\nappear to cite the Act while having read only the Manual. That is a grounding\nfailure that will not show up as a missing source."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/mixedAuthority> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "carries both law and practice"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/mixedAuthority> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/modality> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/modality> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/modality> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "`must` | `may` | `should`, where the relation is normative.\n\n**Absent means not supplied**, and is reported as a gap. It is never inferred\nfrom the sentence's grammar: whether a 'may' is possibility or permission is a\nlegal reading. Five approved relationships carry no modality today and the graph\ncarries none for them."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/modality> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Assertion>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/modality> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "modality"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/modality> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/model> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/model> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The model that produced the assertion, with its version. Absent on an expert-elicited record. HANDOFF Q3 is the question of which model may be named here at all."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/model> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Assertion>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/model> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "model"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/model> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/mustNotConclude> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/mustNotConclude> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The prohibited outputs this question is most likely to provoke. The edge that turns a prohibition from a document into a test."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/mustNotConclude> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "must not conclude"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/mustNotConclude> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ProhibitedUse>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/notLabel> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/notLabel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A term this concept must NOT be conflated with. There is no SKOS property for\nthis and it is the most valuable field on the record.\n\n`deceptively similar` is a not-label of `likely to deceive or cause confusion`\nbecause the two belong to different sections; a retrieval system that treats\nthem as synonyms routes an examiner to the wrong test, and the misrouting is\ninvisible because both destinations are about confusion (GX-0005)."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/notLabel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/LegalConcept>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/notLabel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "not label"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/notLabel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/observedObjectType> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#AnnotationProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/observedObjectType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "As tmk:observedSubjectType, for the object."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/observedObjectType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "observed object type"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/observedSubjectType> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#AnnotationProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/observedSubjectType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A type this predicate's subject has actually taken in the approved set, with no claim that it is the only one. An annotation, so it licenses no inference."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/observedSubjectType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "observed subject type"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/onPage> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/onPage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Chunk>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/onPage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "on page"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/onPage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Page>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ordinal> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ordinal> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ordinal> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Position of a chunk within its page, or a unit within its provision. Reading order, nothing more."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ordinal> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "ordinal"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ordinal> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/origin> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/origin> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/origin> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Which store this node was built from: \"approved\" for eval/gold/, \"authored\" for authored/. Stamped on every node of both, so a triple lifted out of its named graph still says where it came from. The named graph is the governance boundary; this is the belt to its braces (ADR-0080)."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/origin> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/Assertion>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/origin> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "origin"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/origin> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/partId> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/partId> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/partId> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "`Part29`. Comes from the nav tree by way of the ref, never from the URL — deriving it from anything else is how a chunk lands in the wrong Part (Q-09)."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/partId> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Manual Part"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/partId> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/pilotInScope> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/pilotInScope> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "in pilot scope"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/pilotInScope> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/producedByRule> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/producedByRule> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "'Every inferred result identifies the rule that produced it' — one of the six starting SHACL rules, and the reason a rule file carries an id."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/producedByRule> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/InferredAssertion>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/producedByRule> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "produced by rule"@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/prohibitedOutput> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/prohibitedOutput> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The output itself, written out. Kept verbatim because a paraphrase of a prohibited output is not the thing being prohibited."@en-AU  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/prohibitedOutput> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ProhibitedUse>  .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/prohibitedOutput> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "prohibited output"@en-AU  .
