<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s59> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "The registration of a trade mark may be opposed on the ground that the applicant does not intend: (a) to use, or authorise the use of, the trade mark in Australia; or (b) to assign the trade mark to a body corporate for use by the body corporate in Australia; in relation to the goods and/or services specified in the application. Note: For applicant see section 6." <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
