<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/5/5/3/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ordinal> "8"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/5/5/3/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/partId> "Part20" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/5/5/3/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "Where the Registrar or their delegate is satisfied that there is a clear ground for rejecting an application under section 41, the applicant may attempt to overcome that ground for rejection by providing evidence of use or other circumstances. When evidence is required, the onus reverts to the applicant to demonstrate that the trade mark is, or may be taken to be, capable of distinguishing the applicants' goods or services. Part 22 Section 41- Capable of Distinguishing" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/5/5/3/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/upstreamRef> "TMM/Part20/5/5/3/2" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
