<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part23/2/2/3> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/onPage> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part23/2> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part23/2/2/3> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ordinal> "5"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part23/2/2/3> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/partId> "Part23" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part23/2/2/3> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "An applicant may provide the examiner information which provides context to the meaning or use of a particular term in the marketplace. For example, information showing that the applicant’s industry is highly specialised or that the relevant market is very narrow, or that references to a term that appear descriptive are actually ‘trade mark’ use by the applicant, may have a bearing on whether the trade mark actually lacks the necessary capacity to distinguish." <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
