<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part29/5/5/5> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/contentHash> "sha256:c4235ae85720f19a20037d7a4f5a41161ef68438cf8e1ea2d8e36b90b621b1bb" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part29/5/5/5> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/hasCitation> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/cite/TMM/Part29/5/5/5/prov/0> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part29/5/5/5> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "29.5. International Non-Proprietary Names (generic names for pharmaceutical substances) and INN stems" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part29/5/5/5> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "5.5 Section 43 grounds for rejection in relation to INN stems" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part29/5/5/5> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "Part 29 Section 43 - Trade Marks likely to Deceive or Cause Confusion" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part29/5/5/5> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/onPage> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part29/5> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part29/5/5/5> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ordinal> "6"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part29/5/5/5> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/partId> "Part29" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part29/5/5/5> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "A ground for rejection under section 43 exists where a trade mark to be used in relation to pharmaceuticals or veterinary substances consists of an INN stem, or contains a notified INN stem in a meaningful way, and use of the trade mark in respect of the goods covered by the specification are not restricted to substances indicated by the INN stem. A section 43 ground for rejection may be overcome by the applicant agreeing to a condition of registration limiting use of the trade mark to goods containing substances belonging to the relevant INN stem. The endorsement suggested by the Registrar in these circumstances is: It is a condition of registration that any use in respect of pharmaceuticals will be limited to such goods containing substances belonging to the pharmacological group designated by the International Non- Proprietary Name stem <stem>." <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part29/5/5/5> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/upstreamRef> "TMM/Part29/5/5/5" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
