<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part30/3/3/4/1> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "3.4 Copyright Act 1968; Competition and Consumer Act 2010" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part30/3/3/4/1> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "3.4.1 Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander flags" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part30/3/3/4/1> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "30.3. Use contrary to law" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part30/3/3/4/1> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/headingPath> "Part 30 Signs that are Scandalous and Use Contrary to Law" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part30/3/3/4/1> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/onPage> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part30/3> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part30/3/3/4/1> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ordinal> "6"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part30/3/3/4/1> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/partId> "Part30" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part30/3/3/4/1> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "The Prime Minister and Cabinet website of the Honours, Symbols and Legal Policy Branch states that the Australian Aboriginal Flag and Torres Strait Islander Flag are protected by copyright. The Commonwealth owns the copyright in the Aboriginal flag, and allows the design to be freely reproduced by the public except on flags and pennants, banners and buntings. Carroll & Richardson-Flagworld Pty Ltd is the exclusive licensed manufacturer and provider of the Aboriginal Flag on flags and pennants, banners and buntings, and permission to use the Aboriginal Flag in trade marks claiming those goods will need to be sought from them (see the Prime Minister and Cabinet website for contact information). Permission is required from the copyright holder to use the Torres Strait Islander flag in any trade marks claiming any goods or services. Permission can be sought from the Torres Strait Island Regional Council (see the Prime Minister and Cabinet website for contact information). Examiners should consult the IK SME group in relation to any applications which contain the Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander flags or similar images. Note: Grounds for rejection may also arise under section 39 in relation to the Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander flags – see Part 31 Prescribed and Prohibited Signs for more information." <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
