<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part47/1/1/3/1> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/onPage> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part47/1> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part47/1/1/3/1> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/ordinal> "16"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part47/1/1/3/1> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/partId> "Part47" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part47/1/1/3/1> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/text> "The allowable grounds for extending the statutory period to file a notice of intention to oppose or a statement of grounds and particular are: a. an error or omission by the person, the person’s agent, the Registrar or an employee (regs 5.9(4)(a), 17A.34C(4)(a)); b. circumstances beyond the control of the person applying for the extension of time, other than an error or omission by the person, the person’s agent, the Registrar or an employee (regs 5.9(4)(b), 17A.34C(4)(b))." <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part47/1/1/3/1> <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/upstreamRef> "TMM/Part47/1/1/3/1" <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/graph/source> .
